    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **52 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`), following the existing email-validation pattern:\n\n1. **Added a blocklist constant** \u2014 `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS = {mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}` (plus the `java.util.Set` import).\n\n2. **Added the check** in `addOwner`, right after the email is normalized (trimmed + lower-cased) and passes the syntactic `EMAIL_PATTERN` check. If the domain is blocklisted, it returns `400 BAD_REQUEST`.\n\n3. **Added a helper** `isDisposableEmailDomain(email)` that extracts the domain (substring after the last `@`) and checks it against the blocklist.\n\nBecause the check runs on the already-normalized (lower-cased) email, it matches blocklisted domains case-insensitively (e.g. `X@Mailinator.com`). The rule only applies when an email is present, consistent with the endpoint's existing \"email is optional\" behavior.\n\nThe new acceptance test `Cp38Tests.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
